Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: Very well. May I ask my co-counsel, Your Honor, to provide Director Matibag with a comment?

62
00:14:26,300 --> 00:14:31,960
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Assisting counsel for respondent may approach. Likewise, assisting counsel for the prosecutor may approach the witness.

63
00:14:34,540 --> 00:14:52,670
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: Yes, sir. All right. My question is this. Are threats to the life of the vice president constitute a grave offense with far-reaching implications on national stability, public safety, and the continuity of government?

64
00:14:53,370 --> 00:14:55,270
Atty. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Your Honor, objection, please. What

65
00:14:55,270 --> 00:14:56,390
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: is the ground for the objection?

66
00:14:56,670 --> 00:14:58,250
Atty. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: The question of the defense is speculative.

67
00:15:00,950 --> 00:15:02,170
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Overruled. Witness may answer.

68
00:15:03,980 --> 00:15:16,720
Atty. Melvin Matibag: The threat to the President and all other high government officials like the Senate President, the Chief Justice, the Speaker of the House, or any other officers is a threat to the national security and threat to public safety.

69
00:15:17,280 --> 00:15:25,510
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: All right, very well. Now, did you create a special task force to investigate the threats to the life of VP Sara?

70
00:15:26,280 --> 00:15:28,160
Atty. Melvin Matibag: There was none, to my recollection.

71
00:15:32,310 --> 00:15:37,460
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: So let us recall the interview. This is part of

72
00:15:37,460 --> 00:15:56,060
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: an interview of Dempsey Reyes of the Philippine Daily Inquirer. This is part, Your Honor, of Annex G-9 of the Articles of Impeachment. And please direct your attention to paragraph 13 of the minutes of the meeting and allow me to read. Number 13, are you aware of the threats?

73
00:15:56,500 --> 00:15:59,660
Atty. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Your Honor, please, may we confront the witness with the document?

74
00:16:00,760 --> 00:16:01,950
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Very well.

75
00:16:01,960 --> 00:16:07,910
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: Your Honor, we will provide the hard copy and we will display or flash on the screen a soft copy of such document.

76
00:16:08,080 --> 00:16:20,330
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: counsel for both parties may approach the bench and confront the witness with a copy of the document that the counsel for the respondent is referring to. Kindly proceed, counsel. All

77
00:16:20,880 --> 00:16:46,390
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: All right. It says, paragraph 13, or question and answer No. 13: ‘Are you aware of the threats?’ Answer: ‘May press con kasi earlier than that. Sabi niya, parang sabi niya lang, gusto raw siyang patayin daw, according to her new speaker.’ That was during a press conference the day before November 22. So my question is, can you confirm that this is part of the NBI's own records?

78
00:16:47,520 --> 00:16:51,120
Atty. Melvin Matibag: It reflected on the investigation report, so I

79
00:16:51,120 --> 00:16:59,690
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: presume it is. All right. So this is information regarding the threats to the life of VP Sara, is it not?

80
00:17:00,890 --> 00:17:03,570
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Nakalagay po doon, may threat daw po. Tama po.

81
00:17:03,710 --> 00:17:13,420
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: And when you became NBI director in February 2026, did you conduct a motu proprio investigation to help her?

82
00:17:13,800 --> 00:17:36,380
Atty. Melvin Matibag: I was informed by the investigating officers that it was considered the threat that was mentioned to the Vice President. In fact, personalities were subpoenaed, including the Vice President two times, in order to aid the National Bureau of Investigation in this investigation. However, to no avail, there was no attendance from the personalities that were invited.

83
00:17:36,820 --> 00:17:37,090
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: All right.

84
00:17:37,350 --> 00:17:43,950
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: So let me clarify. Under your leadership already, did the NBI subpoena VP Sara for this?

85
00:17:45,200 --> 00:17:55,270
Atty. Melvin Matibag: We never subpoenaed because we noticed that every time a proper subpoena was issued to the Vice President, she would never attend a subpoena.

86
00:17:55,280 --> 00:18:00,230
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: And your basis for saying that is the subpoena connected to the first investigation, correct?

87
00:18:00,640 --> 00:18:10,190
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Not only that. In a lot of proceedings, including the proceeding in the impeachment at the House of Representatives, I noticed that she never attended.

88
00:18:10,200 --> 00:18:15,000
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: So that was your motivation for not issuing a subpoena. Anyway, under your leadership—

89
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:22,950
Atty. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Your Honor, please, may I move to strike from the record the word ‘motivation’? The witness never said ‘motivation.’

90
00:18:22,960 --> 00:18:26,710
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Let it remain in the record. Counsel may proceed.

91
00:18:26,990 --> 00:18:34,670
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: All right. So under your leadership, did the NBI subpoena former Speaker Martin?

92
00:18:34,680 --> 00:18:35,550
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Wala pa po.

93
00:18:35,560 --> 00:18:40,030
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: Wala. But do you intend to issue a subpoena against him?

94
00:18:40,040 --> 00:18:51,270
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Actually, when we're investigating the issue on the 18 Marines, if the 18 Marines were able to issue their statement properly, we intend to subpoena Speaker Martin Romualdez.

95
00:18:51,280 --> 00:19:00,360
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: Okay. So under your leadership, did the NBI subpoena those who were present during that November 22 press conference?

96
00:19:02,120 --> 00:19:08,190
Atty. Melvin Matibag: There are some personalities that were subpoenaed. In fact, I noticed that you presented the subpoenas yesterday.

97
00:19:08,200 --> 00:19:13,630
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: Yeah, but isn't it that those subpoenas were under the leadership of Director Santiago?

98
00:19:13,640 --> 00:19:21,910
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Well, as to the investigation at that time, it had already been the subject of a resolution pending before the Department of Justice.

99
00:19:21,920 --> 00:19:38,920
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: So, in other words, insofar as the alleged threats to the President, there is an ongoing investigation. But in terms of the alleged threats against the Vice President, there's no ongoing investigation.

100
00:19:39,560 --> 00:19:41,260
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Because there is a big difference, Your Honor.

101
00:19:42,140 --> 00:19:51,010
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: Okay. How about Princess Maui, for example, from the November 23 presscon? Was she subpoenaed under your leadership?

102
00:19:51,570 --> 00:19:53,350
Atty. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Ask and answered question, Your Honor.

103
00:19:53,510 --> 00:19:55,850
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: This is the first time about Princess Maui, Your Honor.

104
00:19:56,190 --> 00:19:58,530
Atty. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Your Honor, it has been asked already during the cross.

105
00:19:58,870 --> 00:20:05,750
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: No, the ground is correct. Asked and answered, meaning the witness already answered, no, he did not.

106
00:20:07,220 --> 00:20:08,020
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: All right. But

107
00:20:08,120 --> 00:20:16,750
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: you mentioned a while ago that there were two... Subpoenas issued against VP Sara, correct?

108
00:20:17,010 --> 00:20:17,690
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Yes, sir.

109
00:20:17,750 --> 00:20:19,610
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Based on the record, that was turned over to me.

110
00:20:19,630 --> 00:20:25,650
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: Yeah, but those two subpoenas were issued by former Director NBI Santiago and not under your leadership. By

111
00:20:25,650 --> 00:20:31,110
Atty. Melvin Matibag: the National Bureau of Investigation, yes, under the leadership of Director Santiago.

112
00:20:32,080 --> 00:20:35,310
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: But just to clarify, under your leadership, no subpoena?

113
00:20:35,440 --> 00:20:36,860
Atty. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Asked and answered, Your Honor.

114
00:20:37,360 --> 00:20:38,990
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Asked and answered. Move on, counsel.

115
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:47,800
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: All right, I'll move on. Now, you mentioned yesterday that for grave threats and inciting to sedition, these are still pending before the DOJ.

116
00:20:48,020 --> 00:20:49,200
Atty. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Asked and answered, Your Honor.

117
00:20:50,480 --> 00:20:51,840
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Asked and answered, counsel. Go on.

118
00:20:51,960 --> 00:21:02,840
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: You likewise mentioned yesterday that you have an ongoing investigation. And my question is, is this for the alleged contracting for the assassination?

119
00:21:05,470 --> 00:21:09,010
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Yes, that is very clear. I was able to explain that yesterday.

120
00:21:09,320 --> 00:21:19,070
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: Okay. And particularly, the ongoing investigation pertained to the leads that you have to the alleged person that VP Sara talked to?

121
00:21:19,080 --> 00:21:20,910
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Among others, Your Honor.

122
00:21:20,920 --> 00:21:26,070
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: But no subpoena has been issued to such alleged person under your leadership?

123
00:21:26,080 --> 00:21:31,680
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Because we are under a case build-up status. It is an ongoing investigation, as mentioned yesterday, sir.

124
00:21:31,960 --> 00:21:46,480
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: Okay. Now, let me just clarify. In a subpoena, the NBI must specifically identify the felony or crime for which you are issuing the subpoena. Is that not the case?

125
00:21:46,920 --> 00:21:50,060
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Yes, we provide what is the crime that we will investigate.

126
00:21:50,340 --> 00:21:56,320
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: Okay, very well. So here, what will be the felony or crime that will be indicated in the subpoena?

127
00:21:56,520 --> 00:22:08,760
Atty. Melvin Matibag: But you have to remember, we also have the mandate to protect the Constitution, to protect the peace and order. And if it goes to national security and peace and order, we are also mandated to investigate.

128
00:22:09,040 --> 00:22:12,960
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: Your Honor, with all due respect, Your Honor, the answer was not responsive.

129
00:22:13,460 --> 00:22:15,300
Atty. Melvin Matibag: My answer was very specific.

130
00:22:16,080 --> 00:22:17,980
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: My question was very specific.

131
00:22:18,040 --> 00:22:21,550
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: What will be the felony or crime that will be indicated in the subpoena?

132
00:22:21,550 --> 00:22:33,190
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Witness will please answer. The question was simple. What is the crime, if any, or penalty in relation to the document being asked by the counsel? We all know that there is no crime

133
00:22:33,190 --> 00:22:58,230
Atty. Melvin Matibag: committed when there is a plan to kill until it is executed. But what I'm saying, that's why I'm qualifying, is because one of the mandates of the National Bureau of Investigation is to protect the national security. And we are also mandated to issue a subpoena or an investigation to do so. So if in this case we cannot issue a subpoena, we can issue an invitation for those persons of interest.

134
00:22:59,280 --> 00:23:03,520
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: So, you cannot issue a subpoena, but just an invitation. In other

135
00:23:03,520 --> 00:23:08,000
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: words, this is not under the jurisdiction of the NBI, correct?

136
00:23:08,260 --> 00:23:29,600
Atty. Melvin Matibag: It is within the power of the NBI to protect the national interests and the national security. And as mentioned, there is a continuing threat to the president under Section G, Section 5 of the Republic Act 10867. It is one of the primary duties of the NBI to protect. The security of the president.

137
00:23:29,940 --> 00:23:35,720
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: All right. Yesterday you also mentioned betrayal of public trust, correct?

138
00:23:36,020 --> 00:23:36,580
Atty. Melvin Matibag: That is correct.

139
00:23:36,880 --> 00:23:43,770
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: Can that be indicated in the subpoena when you issue it against this alleged person?

140
00:23:44,860 --> 00:23:55,100
Atty. Melvin Matibag: It can be or it can be not. But why will we put the subject betrayal of public trust if the person being subpoena is not being tried for betrayal of public trust?

141
00:23:56,320 --> 00:24:02,780
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: What if it's against the vice president? Just to clarify, can the subpoena indicate betrayal of public trust?

142
00:24:04,800 --> 00:24:16,820
Atty. Melvin Matibag: We cannot put that because that is not a subject of a case under the reprise penal for a crime. The betrayal of public trust is the variable subject of an impeachment court.

143
00:24:17,140 --> 00:24:24,040
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: All right. So you admit nonetheless that betrayal of public trust is a ground for impeachment, correct?

144
00:24:24,380 --> 00:24:26,280
Atty. Melvin Matibag: That is correct. I think it's in the constitution.

145
00:24:27,560 --> 00:24:37,780
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: Are you saying that once you reach your findings, because we're all waiting for that, is it correct to say that you will file another impeachment case against VP Sara? Oh, thank

146
00:24:37,780 --> 00:24:38,660
Atty. Melvin Matibag: you for that question.

147
00:24:38,820 --> 00:24:40,680
Atty. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Objection, Your Honor. That is speculative.

148
00:24:42,050 --> 00:24:50,170
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: I think the witness is competent enough, and in fact, thank the counsel for the objection.

149
00:24:50,570 --> 00:25:25,350
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Thank you, Mr. Presiding Officer. The betrayal of public trust as the issue in the impeachment court. We don't need to investigate even if we pinpointed the person contracted. Because the point being is the betrayal of public trust was already been consummated. When she publicly admitted, there is already an admission that she contracted a killer, a mamamatay tao or assassin to kill the president. And that itself is already an admission.

