Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Follow-up question, Mr. Witness. According to your testimony yesterday, you reviewed Arturo Las Cañas' affidavit as part of the larger investigation. Concerning the Vice President's capacity to carry out the alleged threat. Sa pagkakaalam po ninyo, Director, at batay din sa larger investigation na iyon, sinagot po ba ng Vice Presidente sa anumang paraan yung mga aligasyon sa affidavit na iyon ni Las Cañas?

421
00:59:53,100 --> 01:00:31,980
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Your Honor, marami po kasi kaming—'yun nga po 'yung gusto kong ipaliwanag—marami po kasi kaming kino-consider na tinatawag natin na open-source intel. 'Yan na po 'yung mga news, mga report. At nung tinitingnan po namin 'yan, si Arturo Lascañas, meron pa po siyang lumabas na balita noon nung isinumite na itong affidavit na ito sa ICC. At naaalala ko po, mayroon din pong lumabas sa balita na mismong si Vice President Sara Duterte, parang sinasabi po niya roon na hindi ko kailangan ng DDS para gumawa ng kayang gawin ng DDS, something to that effect po. Na-consider po namin lahat po 'yan.

422
01:00:32,780 --> 01:00:42,580
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Sa sinabi ninyong sinabi diumano ni Vice President, sinabi niya hindi niya kailangan ang DDS para gawin ang—

423
01:00:42,580 --> 01:00:49,760
Atty. Melvin Matibag: 'Yung kayang gawin ng DDS. Something like that po. Hindi ko po eksaktong ma-recall 'yung phrase na pagkakasabi po.

424
01:00:50,170 --> 01:00:56,150
Sen. Risa Hontiveros: Salamat, Mr. Witness. I may return to that point later.

425
01:00:56,370 --> 01:01:01,110
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: redirect, and recross. When she avails for time, counsel for respondent may proceed.

426
01:01:01,450 --> 01:01:21,650
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: All right, let's go back to the sheriff incident. I'm glad you mentioned history or historical background. Are you aware that that sheriff incident pertains to relief operations that were being conducted by the Vice President, then-Mayor at that time, or Vice Mayor?

427
01:01:22,390 --> 01:01:42,550
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Ang pagkakaalam ko po doon sa balita na iyon, itong sheriff na to is trying to enforce a valid order from a legitimate court. Demolition order po ito na ayaw ipatuloy po ng then mayor and now vice president. So, I might not be aware of a relief operation. Baka po paliwanag po

428
01:01:42,550 --> 01:01:42,910
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: sa akin.

429
01:01:44,550 --> 01:01:54,210
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: I'll just ask you if you're aware. Are you aware that it involved a flash flood? This incident happened after a flash flood in that particular community?

430
01:01:55,010 --> 01:01:57,210
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Hindi po lumabas siya sa balita.

431
01:01:57,210 --> 01:01:59,290
Atty. Melvin Matibag: I have no knowledge of that.

432
01:01:59,980 --> 01:02:05,340
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: Are you aware that VP Sara asked that sheriff for an extension of two hours just to help the victims?

433
01:02:05,660 --> 01:02:07,040
Atty. Melvin Matibag: 'Yun po 'yung lumabas sa balita.

434
01:02:07,420 --> 01:02:17,800
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: And this sheriff and the demolition that you mentioned involved the demolition of informal settlers in that area?

435
01:02:18,560 --> 01:02:22,020
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Opo, kaya po may order of eviction, ibig sabihin po.

436
01:02:22,880 --> 01:02:26,600
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: Are you aware that 30 people died during that incident?

437
01:02:26,980 --> 01:02:28,440
Atty. Melvin Matibag: I have no knowledge of that, Your Honor.

438
01:02:28,640 --> 01:02:39,960
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: So, in other words, are you also aware that it was the sheriff's refusal to provide the two-hour extension—that's why VP Sara got angry?

439
01:02:40,000 --> 01:02:42,520
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Well, that is the claim of the then mayor.

440
01:02:42,740 --> 01:02:43,840
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: If you know only, if you know.

441
01:02:44,680 --> 01:02:45,740
Atty. Melvin Matibag: I have no knowledge.

442
01:02:46,130 --> 01:02:57,610
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: All right, I'll move on to a new point. Now, you also mentioned, to establish this alleged pattern of behavior, the October 18, 2024 press conference, correct?

443
01:02:57,830 --> 01:02:58,230
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Tama po.

444
01:02:58,310 --> 01:03:06,690
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: And this press conference took place, obviously, before the material that you used, or the November 23, 2024 press conference?

445
01:03:06,810 --> 01:03:07,150
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Tama po.

446
01:03:07,290 --> 01:03:23,740
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: All right, I'm showing you a video. Your Honor, we'll just show one video; it's around one minute. This is Exhibit D-4-53 and the USB separately marked as D-4-47. And then I'll ask you questions after this.

447
01:03:23,740 --> 01:03:27,840
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Kindly play the video. The tech through the clerk of court is so directed.

448
01:03:33,250 --> 01:03:46,800
Vice President Sara Zimmerman Duterte: Inulit ng bata, louder this time: ‘Mr. President, can I have your watch as a graduation gift?’ Ang sagot niya—

449
01:03:46,810 --> 01:03:50,120
Vice President Sara Zimmerman Duterte: Why? Why will I give you my watch?

450
01:03:52,120 --> 01:03:59,190
Vice President Sara Zimmerman Duterte: At that point, ay sakit na ako kasi feeling very well.

451
01:04:00,940 --> 01:04:04,420
Vice President Sara Zimmerman Duterte: Nandunin lang ako. Nakakatayo ako dun kasi may gamot ako.

452
01:04:07,150 --> 01:04:10,380
Vice President Sara Zimmerman Duterte: Gusto ko ang ganun yung ulo niya ba.

453
01:04:16,420 --> 01:04:21,270
Vice President Sara Zimmerman Duterte: I realized, toxic na yung relationship.

454
01:04:21,870 --> 01:04:34,080
Vice President Sara Zimmerman Duterte: It did not help na itong dalawang katabi ko tumawa pa. Pinagtawanan pa nila yung bata.

455
01:04:36,860 --> 01:04:48,660
Vice President Sara Zimmerman Duterte: I saw the humiliation sa face ng bata. I wanted to help him. Gusto ko sabihin sa kanya, itong relo ko na lang, relo ito ng vice-presidente, relo ito ng

456
01:04:48,660 --> 01:04:58,880
Vice President Sara Zimmerman Duterte: relo ng presidente, pero I hope this will do. And then I realized na baka mas lalong mapahiya yung bata if I do that. So I just imagined

457
01:05:02,010 --> 01:05:04,830
Vice President Sara Zimmerman Duterte: myself cutting his head.

458
01:05:09,780 --> 01:05:12,160
Vice President Sara Zimmerman Duterte: Gusto ko ganun din ako.

459
01:05:16,210 --> 01:05:19,850
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: First of all, did you watch this whole video, Director Matib?

460
01:05:20,060 --> 01:05:23,200
Atty. Melvin Matibag: I've watched not the entirety of the video.

461
01:05:23,220 --> 01:05:38,860
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: Not the entirety because it's a long video. It's almost two hours. But my question to you is this: is this the video where you based your finding that VP Sara said, ‘Gusto kong tanggalin ang ulo niya,’ imagine cutting his head off? Is this the one?

462
01:05:39,200 --> 01:05:40,960
Atty. Melvin Matibag: 'Yun po. 'Yun po 'yung video na 'yan.

463
01:05:40,960 --> 01:05:46,260
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: And will you agree with—wasn't this press conference heard by the general public?

464
01:05:46,760 --> 01:05:47,180
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Opo.

465
01:05:49,300 --> 01:05:52,860
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: And didn't VP Sara say her statements in jest?

466
01:05:55,200 --> 01:05:56,390
Atty. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: It's speculative, Your Honor.

467
01:05:56,400 --> 01:06:00,150
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: Your Honor, the witness is smart enough and competent enough to answer.

468
01:06:00,160 --> 01:06:01,590
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Nevertheless, Your Honor. Witness may answer.

469
01:06:02,480 --> 01:06:32,260
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Well, again, I will say I cannot go into the state of mind of the Vice President. And precisely the reason why, doon sa pattern of violence, kasama po talaga 'yan, eh, 'yung pag-consider natin. I understand her disgust doon sa nangyari, but probably, pag pinagsama-sama po 'yung aming investigation, mga aming napanood, kasama po 'yan. Doon po namin na-establish 'yung isa doon sa limang factors na pattern of violence.

470
01:06:32,320 --> 01:06:37,920
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: I understand what you're saying, but my question to you is: didn't you take VP Sara's statement out of context?

471
01:06:38,970 --> 01:07:03,630
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Mahirap po para sa aming law enforcement na 'yung ganyang mga statement ay amin pong baliwalain. Katunayan, alam naman po natin, kahit nga biro—halimbawa po, 'yung bomb joke nga po sa eroplano, hinuhuli natin. It's a different thing if you're doing a bomb joke sa eroplano at saka sa open field na kayo lang. Sa amin po sa law enforcement, we have to give credence to that and i-process po namin.

472
01:07:03,870 --> 01:07:17,940
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: So, at any rate, you consider this portion of VP Sara's statement to be grave and serious—to be a grave and serious threat based on the standards that you mentioned yesterday?

473
01:07:18,400 --> 01:07:27,920
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Hindi po 'yun ang sinabi ko. Ang sinabi ko po, kasama siya doon sa kino-consider na marami pong factors para ma-establish po ang pattern of violence.

474
01:07:28,240 --> 01:07:29,460
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: Isn't that kind of a stretch?

475
01:07:30,300 --> 01:07:31,660
Atty. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: It's argumentative, Your Honor.

476
01:07:32,920 --> 01:07:34,820
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Argumentative. Move on, counsel.

477
01:07:35,060 --> 01:07:37,840
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: Nothing further, Your Honor. Salamat po, sir.

478
01:07:37,840 --> 01:07:42,280
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Redirect? Lead prosecutor, any redirect?

479
01:07:45,120 --> 01:07:47,820
Atty. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: Your Honor, may I request for a five-minute break?

480
01:07:50,350 --> 01:08:18,820
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Instead of granting the break, Chair will open the floor for the interjections and interventions of some of the Senator Judges. You have your five minutes, Counsel. Senator Judge Erwin Tulfo, thereafter. Senator Judge Lacson, thereafter. Senator Judge Rafi Tulfo. And hopefully... Senator Judges Villanueva and Pangilinan, that might be in excess of five minutes already. We're making the most out of the five minutes. Just one manifestation,

481
01:08:19,180 --> 01:08:38,950
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: Your Honor, regarding the interpellation of the good Senator Hontiveros, we just want to state for the record, Your Honor, that insofar as the Lascañas affidavit, the Vice President was never given an opportunity to respond to it. Formally. Formally.

482
01:08:40,000 --> 01:08:46,790
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Noted. Senator-Judge—yes, counsel?

483
01:08:46,800 --> 01:08:49,830
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Counsel for the respondent, anything additional?

484
01:08:49,840 --> 01:09:03,470
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: And the VP was also not made to answer to the—what was this? And it was not part of the impeachment complaint, Your Honor, for the record.

485
01:09:03,480 --> 01:09:07,890
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Noted. Noted. Senator-Judge Erwin Tulfo, you have two minutes, sir.

486
01:09:07,900 --> 01:09:09,440
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: you, Mr. Presiding Officer.

487
01:09:11,060 --> 01:09:45,080
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Sa ating testigo, kahapon po nabanggit ninyo na meron na po kayong persons of interest na kinausap na po ng Vice President Sara Duterte para patayin ang Pangulo, First Lady, at former Speaker of the House. Ang tanong ko po, paano pala ninyo ito natuklasan, natunton ang impormasyong ito? Gayong sa kanya pong press conference, wala naman po siyang sinabi kung sino ang mga taong ito. Sinabi niya lang na may kinausap na po siya. How did you find out?

488
01:09:46,480 --> 01:10:21,520
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Ganito po 'yan. Sa lahat naman po ng kaso na hinahawakan po ng National Bureau of Investigation, para po maging successful 'yung aming pag-imbestiga, nagre-rely po kami sa iba't ibang intelligence report. May tinatawag na open-source intel, human intelligence, and we also use tools to monitor things. At nag-trim down po tayo niyan; tinitingnan po natin hanggang dumating tayo doon sa punto na mayroon pong resolusyon 'yung ating pong kasong tinitingnan with regards to persons of interest. 'Yung prosesong din 'yan po ang ating pong sinundan.

489
01:10:22,340 --> 01:10:49,160
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Okay. Without mentioning po kung sino itong mga tao na ito, or 'yung pagkakilanlan nila, kung nasaan sila, maaari po ba ninyong bigyan kami ng idea itong mga persons of interest na ito, kung ano po talaga ang trabaho nila? Kung sila po ba talaga mga hitman, o mga gun for hire, o riding in tandem? Ano po ang klaseng trabaho mayroon itong mga ito?

490
01:10:49,520 --> 01:11:31,620
Atty. Melvin Matibag: ang tinatawag na connection, yung network po. Alam naman natin na siya ay

491
01:11:31,620 --> 01:12:29,930
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Vice President, at ang dating Pangulo ay kanyang ama. Ibig sabihin, nakadevelop po ito ng mga relasyon, unang-una na sa mga men in uniform na hanggang sa ngayon, marami po rito na na-appoint pa niya noong panahon na sila ay nandoon. Nabanggit ko rin 'yung Vice Presidential Security Group at 'yung mga Davao Death Squad. So tiningnan po natin, by process of elimination, 'yung mga tao po na maaaring doon nanggaling o maaaring nakakaalam. Nag-start po kami sa maraming individuals hanggang sa ma-trim down po namin ngayon. Kaya sinabi ko po kahapon sa katanungan ng ating Senate President, ganoon ba katagal pa ito? And I said we have great progress. Dahil nagsimula po kami sa marami, ngayon na-trim down na po namin sa iilang personalidad po.

492
01:12:30,880 --> 01:12:47,520
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Okay. Pangalawa sa huling katanungan ko po, Ginoong Testigo, ay itong threat na ito. Ito po hanggang ngayon ay continuing threat po ito, or puwedeng i-execute anytime ng mga sinasabi ninyong persons of interest?

493
01:12:48,420 --> 01:13:12,570
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Yun na po yung ating pong pangamba na nakikita. Because hindi po natin nakukuha, sigurado po tayo na may kinausap at pumayang, subalit yung pagkakakilanlan ng taong kinausap ay hindi pa rin po natin nakukuha. So ibig sabihin po, yung threat po na ito sa Pangulo is a continuing and active threat, po in serious. So yun po yung gusto nating i-address dito.

494
01:13:13,390 --> 01:13:24,900
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Panguling katanungan na lamang, Mr. Witness. Na-informa na po ba ang Pangulo at ang kanyang PSG para alam nila ang kanilang gagawin at hindi po sila malingat sa kanilang siguridad?

495
01:13:25,500 --> 01:13:38,020
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Meron po kaming tuloy-tuloy na pakikipag-ugnayan sa palasyo po. I will not mention who exactly yung mga kausap po namin doon but there's always continuing threat assessment po na ginagawa po kami.

496
01:13:38,320 --> 01:13:40,640
Sen. Erwin Tulfo: Thank you Mr. Witness. Presiding Officer, thank you.

497
01:13:40,660 --> 01:14:00,930
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Thank you Sen. Judge Erwin Tulfo, Sen. Judge Lacson. Thereafter, we will recognize first with the indulgence of Senator Judge Rafi Tulfo, the lead prosecutor for her manifestation. As I understand, she asked for time for a huddle to determine whether she will still conduct redirects. So, Senator Judge Lacsonas, recognized. You have two minutes,

498
01:14:01,720 --> 01:14:55,120
Sen. Panfilo M. Lacson: Thank you, sir, Presiding Officer. Follow-up lang ito sa mga points raised by Senator-Judge Raffy Tulfo kahapon relating to three similar cases: Ronel Mas, Mayor Baste Duterte, saka VP Sara. Hindi ko na ibe-belabor 'yung Ronel Mas and Mayor Baste kasi aware naman ako doon sa Rule 113, Section 5, 'yung warrantless arrest, na hindi puwedeng i-apply. Nagkamali nga 'yung NBI kay Ronel Mas, kaya na-dismiss 'yung case, 'di po ba? But I'm more interested in the cases of Mayor Baste at saka kay VP Sara, kasi almost similar 'yung kanilang mga sinabi. Pero I'm just wondering why you did not investigate Mayor Baste, pero si Mayor Sara, hindi lang kayo nag-investigate, nag-prepare pa kayo ng complaint sa DOJ, 'di po ba?

499
01:14:55,940 --> 01:15:16,980
Atty. Melvin Matibag: 'Yan po 'yung aming ginawang investigation ay doon na po sa threat na sinasabi namin na pangkalawakan. 'Yung dito po kay Mayor Baste, kaya hindi po natin iniimbestigahan, isinasama po namin dito sa task force na ito to come out with the report eventually. But we have coordination also po with other agencies.

500
01:15:17,380 --> 01:15:22,760
Sen. Panfilo M. Lacson: Yes. So walang ongoing law-enforcement investigation against Mayor Baste?

501
01:15:23,200 --> 01:15:27,540
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Kasama po dito sa special task force po.

502
01:15:28,520 --> 01:15:44,100
Sen. Panfilo M. Lacson: 'Yung bang Special Task Force—and this was also raised by the Presiding Officer nung nasa lounge kami kanina—na-form ba ito in relation to or in reference to the case of Mayor Baste o kay Vice President Sara?

503
01:15:44,500 --> 01:16:15,180
Atty. Melvin Matibag: 'Yung pong trigger point na nangyari dito ay 'yung pong kay Mayor Baste po. But prior to that, we were continually monitoring the threat. Kasama po sa aming pag-uusap 'yan. In fact, 'yung pong aming reporting of records, as early as noong nag-assume po ako ng February, mga first week pa lang po ng March, kasama na po sa reporting 'yung mga threat assessment. But nung napansin po namin na itong rage rally na ito can escalate to a bigger threat to national security, doon po namin ipinasok ito.

504
01:16:15,400 --> 01:16:24,590
Sen. Panfilo M. Lacson: So mas ang ginamit ninyo 'yung kay Mayor Baste as an open source, kaysa sa mag-file kayo ng criminal complaint against Mayor Baste?

505
01:16:24,600 --> 01:16:39,070
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Ganoon po 'yung naging process namin dito. But eventually, we have an agreement within us that if we can establish that the elements for grave threats will be there, we will be contemplating also filing grave threats and inciting to sedition as well.

506
01:16:39,270 --> 01:17:21,820
Sen. Panfilo M. Lacson: Pero halos pareho, eh. Kaya iniisip ko baka merong double standard. Bakit kaya nag-focus kay Vice President, pero hindi n'yo in-apply kay Mayor Baste? Eh halos pareho ang sinabi nila. Maliwanag naman, bukod doon sa January 2026, naulit pa ng April 12, di ba, na sinabing [unclear], threat against the first family; nasundan pa ng ‘pupugot, ang kailangan lang namin 'yung ulo.’ Pero kay Vice President, halos ganoon din, eh. Pero bakit inimbestigahan n'yo si Vice President Sara at na-refer n'yo na sa DOJ for preliminary investigation, pero 'yung kay Mayor Baste, parang uneven, nasa law-enforcement investigation pa rin?

507
01:17:22,540 --> 01:17:40,200
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Sapagkat ang isa pong dine-develop namin dito na theory po is 'yung sabwatan. And alam po natin, if we go to court using the theory of conspiracy, medyo mas mahirap po na ipasok na kaso. So kaya it's taking much time to develop the case po.

508
01:17:40,200 --> 01:17:43,620
Sen. Panfilo M. Lacson: May request for additional time, Mr. Presiding Officer. Punta lang kay Lascañas.

509
01:17:43,620 --> 01:17:43,880
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Opo.

510
01:17:43,880 --> 01:17:49,870
Sen. Panfilo M. Lacson: Okay. 'Yung kay Lascañas, ginamit ninyo 'yung kanyang affidavit na isinumite sa ICC.

511
01:17:50,650 --> 01:17:51,490
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Tama po.

512
01:17:51,890 --> 01:17:55,150
Sen. Panfilo M. Lacson: Parang pang open source. Not for anything, di ba?

513
01:17:55,310 --> 01:17:56,330
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Not for anything po.

514
01:17:56,350 --> 01:17:57,930
Sen. Panfilo M. Lacson: So walang evidentiary value ito?

515
01:17:58,330 --> 01:18:07,530
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Yun po ay ang basehan namin, kaya po namin iprinisinta. Isa po sa naging basehan namin dun po sa isa nga dun sa five standards po natin na pattern of violence po.

516
01:18:07,750 --> 01:18:17,000
Sen. Panfilo M. Lacson: Pero wala kayong intention na kung magpapile kayo ng kaso, As a

517
01:18:17,000 --> 01:18:29,300
Atty. Melvin Matibag: As a matter of reference lang po, for the purpose of establishing the pattern of violence. But to directly papanagutin po sa isang krimen or what, eh sa palagay ko po baka po hindi ito tatanggapin ng korte po.

518
01:18:29,380 --> 01:18:32,320
Sen. Panfilo M. Lacson: Yeah, kasi kung open source, hindi nga tatanggapin ng korte.

519
01:18:32,360 --> 01:18:32,760
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Tama po.

520
01:18:32,900 --> 01:19:09,580
Sen. Panfilo M. Lacson: Kasi kung open source, kung nag-extend pa kayo and expanded 'yung open-source information gathering, dapat sana na-review ninyo rin 'yung aming committee hearing dito. 'Yung na-mention kanina ng defense na initially deny nang deny talaga si Arturo Lascañas tungkol sa DDS, EJK, et cetera. Eventually, nag-retract siya, talagang 180 degrees. Sinabi niya, totoo 'yung EJK. Hindi ba dapat part din 'yon ng open-source information gathering ninyo?

521
01:19:09,580 --> 01:19:39,360
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Tama po. Actually, nung binasa po namin 'yung affidavit, may isang paragraph doon na nagtukoy nga diyan na nag-testify at saka binawi. Ang sinundan na po namin dito—at naalala ko po, meron kasing news report doon sa 24 Oras after ng pre-trial po sa ICC—nagkaroon po ng interview kay Lascañas kung saan sinasabi niya 'yung affidavit na ginawa niya na isinumite sa ICC. At nung kinukumpara po namin doon sa sinasabi niya, lumalabas na 'yun po. Pangatlo na po 'yun.

522
01:19:39,360 --> 01:20:19,750
Sen. Panfilo M. Lacson: So alam ninyo, iba 'yung affidavit niya, 'yung kanyang testimony sa Public Order and Dangerous Drugs Committee, which, as I said earlier, I chaired. Kaya alam ko, familiar ako. Then after that, nag-retract siya, talagang complete turnaround. So I even consulted a retired justice na kaibigan ko: ano bang mas matimbang dito? Ang sabi niya, talagang jurisprudence, 'yung original na statement ang mananaig kaysa doon sa parang binaligtad na statement, which I also agreed. Ang point ko lang is, bakit parang namili lang kayo ng open source?

523
01:20:20,580 --> 01:20:37,130
Sen. Panfilo M. Lacson: Kung titingnan ninyo 'yung sa ICC na isinumite na pagkahaba-haba, sa akin nga po sinabi kanina, pangatlo na po 'yung magkakaibang affidavits ni Arturo Lascañas. May nauna, may pangalawa. Pangatlo na po itong pinapakita sa screen kahapon.

524
01:20:37,370 --> 01:21:07,680
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Tama po. And we are also aware doon sa pagbalibaligtad. But on the news that I was mentioning po, Your Honor, mismong sinabi niya, pipirmahan 'yung affidavit, at sinabi po niya, ‘This is 186 pages.’ So nung tinitingnan po namin 'yung statement na iyan, tumugma. At pangalawa, it's been the subject already of an ICC. It's being used as evidence. At least there is a legitimate court that's looking into it. It was considered—ibig sabihin, tinanggap po ng isang legitimate na korte po.

525
01:21:08,080 --> 01:21:18,320
