840
02:26:20,640 --> 02:26:53,570
Sen. Imee Marcos: So ang sinasabi po ninyo, tama 'yung pagka-file pero hindi kumpleto 'yung mga findings doon sa affidavit of investigation, dahil 'yan din ang sinabi ni NBI Agent Lotoc na nandito. Ipinahiwatig niya na siya'y lead investigator, pero wala siyang personal knowledge of whether there was an actual assassin. So why is it that 14 months after filing of the cases, the assassin is yet to be named? At ngayon, humihingi pa kayo ng three to six months para tuklasin kung sino nga 'yun?

841
02:26:54,440 --> 02:27:06,760
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Ganito nga po: 'yung pong grave threats at inciting to sedition, nandoon na po sa DOJ 'yan. That is the subject of a resolution na dapat gawin ng DOJ. Magkaiba po 'yan; ihiwalay po natin.

842
02:27:07,080 --> 02:27:23,480
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Ito pong ating investigation dito is an investigation because of the continuing active and serious threat to the President, amounting to the effect na 'yung national security is being compromised. So doon po natin tinitingnan.

843
02:27:23,770 --> 02:28:21,690
Sen. Imee Marcos: Hindi po 'yan ang sinabi ninyo, eh. Kasi ang sinabi ninyo doon sa House of Representatives, sa Justice Committee, eh maliwanag. Sabi ninyo, mayroon kaming leads at mukhang ito na talaga ang findings. Kaya nga po nag-file ng kaso ng grave threats at inciting to sedition. Sabi ninyo, 'yan ang dahilan. That was your statement. Because if you stand by these words, na may finding na talaga, at 'yun ang dahilan kaya nag-file noong February. As early as February, the date that the NBI filed, the NBI already had findings that VP Sara spoke with an assassin. How come? Kaya ngayon sinasabi ninyo na wala naman noong panahon na 'yun; ganoon din ang sinabi ni Atty. Lotoc. So hindi ko maintindihan ngayon, talaga bang may assassin na na-identify noong Pebrero o wala?

844
02:28:22,030 --> 02:28:24,370
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Wala pong na-identify nung Pebrero.

845
02:28:24,670 --> 02:28:32,310
Sen. Imee Marcos: Eh bakit ninyo sinabi doon sa House of Representatives na yung dahilan na

846
02:28:32,990 --> 02:28:37,480
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Ah, that is it. Totally magkaiba po na issue. Again, babalik po ako.

847
02:28:37,560 --> 02:28:49,480
Sen. Imee Marcos: Pareho yung issue eh kasi yun din ang inaalam ng Justice Committee noon eh. At ang liwa-liwanag na sabi niyo yung dahilan na nakapagpila na sila ay dahil natuklasan na yung asasin.

848
02:28:50,140 --> 02:29:00,300
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Wala po akong sinabi doon na natuklasan. I also mentioned at that time that there are persons of interest. Again, we have to go back po doon sa inciting to sedition and grave threats.

849
02:29:00,680 --> 02:29:01,820
Sen. Imee Marcos: Tama po 'yung transcript kasi.

850
02:29:02,040 --> 02:29:04,100
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Okay po, tama naman po 'yung binabasa niya.

851
02:29:04,260 --> 02:29:10,860
Sen. Imee Marcos: Kaya nga nag-file ng kaso kasi mayroon na kaming leads. Ang liwanag ng pagkasabi ninyo, eh.

852
02:29:11,360 --> 02:29:30,620
Atty. Melvin Matibag: We are referring—may lead na nga po. Ibig sabihin, 'yung pong grave threat, completed na, eh. Mayroon nang threat. In fact, tumatawid na po tayo sa may kinausap. And we are already talking about, nandito sa admission ni Vice President Sara, na mayroon siyang kinausap na papatay at pumayag 'yung papatay.

853
02:29:31,100 --> 02:29:50,000
Sen. Imee Marcos: Parang napakalinaw noong sinabi n'yo noon at mas malabo di-hamak ngayon. Ngayon, bakit kailangan pang mag-issue ng AO 11? Kung talaga namang continuing investigation, dahil ba ito sa April 12, 'yung sinasabi n'yong Rage Coalition?

854
02:29:50,960 --> 02:30:01,680
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Kasama po 'yan. Paulit-ulit ko pong sinasabi na there are five points na tiningnan po natin na ginagamit po ng isang security service.

855
02:30:01,700 --> 02:30:07,500
Sen. Imee Marcos: Yes, we're aware of that: the social, economic, et cetera. Alam naman natin 'yun kasi 'yan din ang gamit ng U.S., 'di ba?

856
02:30:07,500 --> 02:30:18,680
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Tama po. Kaya po may ongoing investigation. Sinabi ko na 'yung threat is serious, continuing, and active, na ito po ay tumatawid na rin to the level of national security.

857
02:30:19,000 --> 02:30:24,500
Sen. Imee Marcos: Kung talagang may pattern of violence, doon sa Rage Coalition launching, andun ba si VP Sara?

858
02:30:25,380 --> 02:30:26,060
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Wala po.

859
02:30:26,970 --> 02:30:33,330
Sen. Imee Marcos: As a matter of fact, she wasn't even there. Siya ba nagsalita? Siya ba nagsabi noon?

860
02:30:33,850 --> 02:30:35,450
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Si Mayor Baste po.

861
02:30:35,890 --> 02:30:41,650
Sen. Imee Marcos: Are you implying na may conspiracy kay VP Sara at Mayor Baste to have the President killed?

862
02:30:41,920 --> 02:30:48,820
Atty. Melvin Matibag: 'Yan po 'yung aming tinitingnan. Kanina po, tanong ni Senator Ping Lacson, tinitingnan po natin kung may sabwatan po na nangyayari.

863
02:30:49,120 --> 02:31:00,200
Sen. Imee Marcos: May katibayan ba tayo dito sa conspiracy? Dahil matindi ang pinag-aralan niyo bilang abogado. Sapat ba ito para ipakita na may conspiracy dun sa dalawa?

864
02:31:00,400 --> 02:31:19,800
Atty. Melvin Matibag: 'Yun po rin 'yung sagot ko kanina kay Senator Ping Lacson. Kaya po hindi pa nakasuhan sapagkat, tulad po ng mga kaso na pumapasok at alam po ng mga abogado, conspiracy is sometimes harder to prove than the crime itself. That's why we have to make a case build-up para masiguro po natin ang isasampang kaso.

865
02:31:19,800 --> 02:31:23,420
Sen. Imee Marcos: Sa madaling sabi, wala pa pong katibayan ng conspiracy.

866
02:31:24,220 --> 02:31:27,340
Atty. Melvin Matibag: 'Yun po 'yung tinitingnan nga nating anggulo kaya tinitingnan natin.

867
02:31:27,340 --> 02:31:31,240
Sen. Imee Marcos: 'Yun nga, pero sa ngayon, habang tayo ang naglilitis dito, wala pa.

868
02:31:31,240 --> 02:31:40,680
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Kung mayroon na po, nai-file na po namin 'yan. Kailangan po lumusot ito under Memorandum Circular No. 20 of the Department of Justice, reasonable certainty of conviction.

869
02:31:40,680 --> 02:32:01,250
Sen. Imee Marcos: Alam natin 'yan. Ang sabi ninyo, 'yung Special Task Force, ano ang gagawin ng Special Task Force kung natumbok na rin 'yung assassin noong Pebrero pa? O natumbok na ninyo ngayon na nasa ilan na na-interview ninyo? Ano ang gagawin sa mga assassin na ito?

870
02:32:01,530 --> 02:32:11,930
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Then, kailangan po natin silang imbistigad at kausapin kung gaano kalawak para malaman po natin kung huminto na ba ang threat sa Presidente sa pagkatalamin natin kung sino po ang makakausap.

871
02:32:12,200 --> 02:32:31,220
Sen. Imee Marcos: Dahil maraming nagtatanong kung bakit pa kailangan mag-case build-up samantalang eto na tayo sa impeachment trial, eto na tayo na wala pang actual assassination, kaya hindi naman maintindihan kung ano pa ang silbi ng Special Task Force.

872
02:32:31,720 --> 02:33:03,640
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Alam po ninyo, dito po sa impeachment, mag-iba po 'yung requirement. Sa Impeachment Court, hindi naman po necessary na may criminal conviction. Kaya po inilatag po 'yan kung ano-ano 'yung mga basehan po.

873
02:33:04,000 --> 02:33:41,000
Sen. Imee Marcos: Sa ating Presiding Judge at pati na rin kay Atty. Matibag, ang ating director: sabi po ninyo na matutumbok ninyo ito sa loob ng tatlo hanggang anim na buwan. Kung maaari, sabihin na ninyo sa amin. Puwede naman i-disclose kung tutuusin at sasampahan naman niya ng demanda through regular filing, hindi dito sa impeachment, at hindi naman siya subject of arrest for inquest proceeding. Bakit hindi sabihin? Or kung maaari, bumalik na lang kayo in three to six months. Puwede bang i-request 'yon kapag mayroon na kayong natuklasan at napuntiryang assassin?

874
02:33:41,330 --> 02:34:27,760
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Again, ang sagot ko po diyan, iba po naman 'yung national security protection and impeachment. Dito po sa impeachment, 'yung sinasabing betrayal of public trust ay pumasok na po dahil mayroon pong sinumpaang tungkulin ang ating Vice President to protect and defend the Constitution, execute the law, do justice to everyone, and consecrate herself to the service of the nation. Alam po natin 'yan. Eh 'yung pong ginawa niya po, papasok po 'yun sa betrayal of public trust kasi enforce the law, do justice, pero ito po, execute the law—ito, execute the President po. Alam po natin 'yan. Pero binubuo natin ang mga elemento ng grave threats at inciting to sedition.

875
02:34:27,760 --> 02:34:28,500
Sen. Imee Marcos: Maraming salamat.

876
02:34:28,500 --> 02:34:34,000
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Thank you, Senator-Judge Imee. Any other Senator-Judge who wishes to make an interjection?

877
02:34:35,560 --> 02:34:42,020
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Unless Senator-Judge [unclear] will have some interjections, then—

878
02:34:46,700 --> 02:35:00,600
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Just a few questions. Annika, kindly turn on the timer too, just to be sure that I'm within the time. Director Matibag, ito ba ang unang pagkakataon na may binuong task force para mag-imbestiga sa mga banta laban sa Pangulo?

879
02:35:01,600 --> 02:35:03,140
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Sa pagkaalala ko po, oo po.

880
02:35:03,320 --> 02:35:04,720
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Sa kasaysayan ng NBI?

881
02:35:05,140 --> 02:35:08,260
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Based on the records turned over to me, wala po.

882
02:35:08,500 --> 02:35:19,770
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Hindi po ba normal, regular, at ordinaryo lamang na magkaroon ng banta? Ang Pangulo, Ikalawang Pangulo, o sinumang mataas na opisyal, o sinumang mayaman dito sa ating bansa, kaya may mga bodyguards sila, 'di ba?

883
02:35:20,090 --> 02:35:24,810
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Tama po yan. Araw-araw po ay alam natin na may threat, pero magkakaibang level po.

884
02:35:25,050 --> 02:35:35,390
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Tama po yun. At kung may mga threat tulad nito, at kung ito ang unang pagkakataong ginawa ito ng NBI, ang humahawak ng mga bantang ito ay ang PSC na, o PSG dati. Tama po ah?

885
02:35:35,490 --> 02:35:38,270
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Tama po. Kaya po mayroon po kaming coordination po.

886
02:35:38,290 --> 02:35:57,550
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Tutumbukin ko na po 'yung mga punto ko para hindi ako lumampas sa oras na sinusunod ng lahat. Sa inyong investigation, may bayad po ba 'yung kinausap ni VP Sara, kung 100% certain po kayo na may kinausap siya para patayin diumano ang Pangulo? May bayad po ba iyon o libre?

887
02:35:57,790 --> 02:36:01,570
Atty. Melvin Matibag: That is the part of the investigation po that we have to establish po.

888
02:36:01,830 --> 02:36:08,950
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: So sa ngayon hindi pa po ninyo sigurado kung pagkakaibigan lang o samahan lang o may bayad 'yung usapang iyon?

889
02:36:09,190 --> 02:36:11,510
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Tama po, but we consider every possibility.

890
02:36:12,050 --> 02:36:40,990
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Ngayon, would it matter, Director Matibag, kung sino 'yung sinabihan niya? Kasama po sa lima ninyong pamantayan na binanggit po ninyo ay identity of person involved and capacity. Halimbawa po, kung ang kinausap ng Ikalawang Pangulo ay kaklase niya sa college na nagtatrabaho sa call center, relevant po ba't mahalaga iyon? Kaugnay ng capacity, hindi ba? At kaugnay ng identity ng taong kinausap?

891
02:36:41,170 --> 02:36:43,450
Atty. Melvin Matibag: That will be considered in the investigation po.

892
02:36:43,710 --> 02:36:48,070
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Sa ibig sabihin, hindi po iyon babagsak sa valid threat, hindi po ba?

893
02:36:48,810 --> 02:36:54,010
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Hindi po natin alam at kailangan pong alamin kung ano 'yung pag-uusap o ano po ang mga konsiderasyon. Pero—

894
02:36:54,010 --> 02:37:01,630
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Pero base sa inyong karanasan po, kung retired police, retired military, active police, marahil may punto kayo, hindi po ba?

895
02:37:01,630 --> 02:37:02,830
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Mas malaki po ang posibilidad.

896
02:37:03,310 --> 02:37:15,690
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Pero kung walang military background, walang background kaugnay sa paggamit ng anumang uri ng armas o walang background kaugnay sa anumang karahasang nagawa na niya sa kapwa niya, may basehan din po iyon para sabihin iyong kabaliktaran, hindi po ba?

897
02:37:16,390 --> 02:37:17,810
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Titignan po natin. Tama po.

898
02:37:18,290 --> 02:37:31,070
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: At bilang panghuling katanungan, ito pong inyong task force ay binuo para imbestigahan ang mga banta laban sa Pangulo. Wala na po itong kinalaman sa Ikalawang Pangulo mismo kaugnay ng mga kasong isinampa laban sa kanya na grave threats at inciting to sedition?

899
02:37:31,250 --> 02:37:32,150
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Tama po, Your Honor.

900
02:37:32,700 --> 02:37:45,620
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Thank you, Director Matibag. Unless there are any other questions—Senator-Judge Legarda, I'm sorry, you are recognized. I thought there was no other Senator-Judge, that's why I already interjected. Senator-Judge Legarda, for her interjection.

901
02:37:47,870 --> 02:37:52,110
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Senator-Judge Legarda, you have two minutes, ma'am.

902
02:37:57,150 --> 02:38:05,720
Sen. Loren Legarda: I guess I'm the last to ask. I don't know why the majority senators, macho bloc, don't want me to ask simple questions on national security.

903
02:38:06,220 --> 02:38:54,920
Sen. Loren Legarda: No, this is levity aside. It's a barkada talk. It's very simple. I studied national security. I'm a graduate of my master's in national security. I was discussing it with former General Lacson, Senator Lacson, because the words ‘national security’ have been used many times in this hall in the past few days. So my questions are very simple. Just for the record, he's my friend, my compadre, Director Melvin Matibag, and Congresswoman Ann. Okay. So hindi po dahil nagpapalambot ako dahil kumpare ko siya. Gusto ko lang ipahayag ang simpleng katanungan dahil madalas n'yong ginagamit ang national security. At alam ito ni Melvin, I'm a national security expert, graduate. I studied it.

904
02:38:55,480 --> 02:39:32,580
Sen. Loren Legarda: Batay po sa inyong kaalaman, records o ebidensyang nakalap, may koordinasyon po ba ang NBI sa iba pang ahensyang may kaugnayan dahil sa mga alleged na pahayag ng ating Vice President?

905
02:39:33,000 --> 02:39:56,900
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Mayroon po akong pakikipag-usap po sa PSC. May coordination kami. Katunayan, 'yung aming ibang inaksyunan ay base po sa intel report po sa amin ng PSC, ng Presidential Security Command. At mayroon din nga po ako, nabanggit ko na kanina, pakikipag-ugnayan po sa military at sa security cluster through the Executive Secretary po.

906
02:39:57,960 --> 02:40:17,070
Sen. Loren Legarda: So, all of these discussions, are there issuances, memoranda, notices, minutes, directives, reports, official documentation na nagpapatunay sa naturang coordination ng task force?

907
02:40:17,610 --> 02:40:23,230
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Yung pong aking mga report ay akin pong isinusumite through the Office of Executive Secretary po.

908
02:40:23,900 --> 02:40:40,720
Sen. Loren Legarda: How long have you had this interagency task force and is there such a name of a task force? Where was it? Kailan po tinatag? Kailan natapos? Was there a terminal report? And would you consider it, you've always said, it's a national security concern?

909
02:40:41,220 --> 02:40:53,950
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Well, there's no specific task force but the coordination, as I said, is to the Executive Secretary but we are also coordinating with the Presidential Security Command and on the military group.

910
02:40:54,850 --> 02:41:10,410
Sen. Loren Legarda: Mr. Presiding Officer, would the reports of the interagency task force na tinatag ng NBI be given to the body so that we have an idea of the investigations conducted by the NBI? Has it been submitted?

911
02:41:11,890 --> 02:41:19,850
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Let the Presiding Officer make a distinction. Again, The court should be a passive body. We should be receiving evidence through the

912
02:41:19,850 --> 02:41:32,470
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: of counsel of the parties. Unless someone would present it, the Court should simply await its submission, if at all, through the parties.

913
02:41:32,690 --> 02:41:49,530
Sen. Loren Legarda: So my question would be: was this submitted as part of your evidence, the terminal report and the investigations conducted by this interagency body? Because it's the first time I'm actually realizing that there was such an interagency body and that this was actually discussed in the National Security Council?

914
02:41:49,530 --> 02:42:10,610
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Well, sabi ko nga po, through the Executive Secretary, we have been making reports, and for reasons that I mentioned yesterday, that I cannot give the reports that are confidential in nature, ay hindi ko po ito maibahagi sa Impeachment Court po na ito.

915
02:42:11,110 --> 02:42:19,650
Sen. Loren Legarda: So wala pong pinabigyan, maski anong mga kopya na reports, even just a summation of all these investigations. It was

916
02:42:19,650 --> 02:42:21,770
Atty. Melvin Matibag: given po to the Executive Secretary po.

917
02:42:21,870 --> 02:42:23,310
Sen. Loren Legarda: And this court has a...

918
02:42:23,310 --> 02:42:24,170
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Wala po.

919
02:42:24,230 --> 02:42:33,870
Sen. Loren Legarda: No copy of it. Therefore, I would terminate my questions here. And if we don't have a copy of that report, then we leave it at that. Thank you very much.

920
02:42:34,010 --> 02:42:51,030
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Salamat po. Thank you, Senator Judge Legarda. If there are no other Senator Judges who wishes to make interjections, Is there anything that either of the Council for the Parties wish to state before we adjourn? Atty. Vidluan, I

921
02:42:51,030 --> 02:42:53,190
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: see you standing up. If

922
02:42:53,290 --> 02:43:14,320
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: there are none, Chair would now like to dispose of some administrative matters. First, the Chair would like to remind the parties in connection with the conference for the marking and or transfer of markings and comparison of video exhibits. Tomorrow at 10 a.m. at Director Room, this shall proceed.

923
02:43:16,500 --> 02:43:18,280
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Senator Judge Soto, what is your pleasure, sir?

924
02:43:18,420 --> 02:43:23,680
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: I'm sorry, Your Honor. Kind sir, won't we dispose of the witness first?

925
02:43:24,600 --> 02:43:25,820
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: You're correct, Your Honor.

926
02:43:26,680 --> 02:43:27,220
Sen. Vicente C. Sotto III: Thank you.

927
02:43:28,200 --> 02:43:36,500
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: If there are no further questions, Director Matibag, you're excused, sir. Thank you for your time. Thank you for your cooperation. And thank you for your patience as well.

928
02:43:36,940 --> 02:43:38,800
Atty. Melvin Matibag: Salamat din po. Magandang hapon po.

929
02:43:38,900 --> 02:46:44,700
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Thank you po. Magandang hapon po. To restate, the conference tomorrow at 10 a.m. The parties are duly reminded at the Recto Room. Number two, subpoenas shall be issued. The Clerk of Court is directed to issue a subpoena to Ms. Violeta Constantino, former Land Bank manager, and Ms. Nenita Camposano, former branch manager also of Land Bank, for the resumption of trial on Wednesday, July 29 at 10 a.m., unless the court issues a subsequent order recalling or changing the date of the same. And one last point administratively: the Chair would like to remind the parties to this case of Article 18, pertaining to the rule on making comments or disclosures on the part of the prosecutors, counsel for respondent, and their witnesses. I say this because I noticed that Atty. Tolosa, who is a registered counsel for the panel of prosecutors, and Atty. Poa, who is a registered counsel for the respondent, are both serving as the spokespersons as well. Thus far, both have been very careful, but as the trial goes on, it might take its toll with respect to the spokespersons and counsels at the same time being able to distinguish between the merits of the case and purely procedural observations and/or facts. So you might want to consider, in order to give a freer hand, nominating a spokesperson that is purely a spokesperson, who is not limited by the rules of the Impeachment Court with respect to what he or she can say. Because, for your information, the Court will be monitoring the statements being issued by the counsels for the parties, for the information and guidance of the counsels. And since this is the last witness of the panel of prosecutors for Article IV, the Chair would like to inform the Senator-Judges that the pretrial order allocated 11 days for the presentation of this article by the panel of prosecutors. They actually consumed only six days, given the withdrawal of certain witnesses. We consumed three days for oral arguments on the subpoena, on the interjections and debates with senators, and on the opening statements of the parties. A total of nine days have been spent, therefore, since we started. So we are still ahead by two days based on the timetable given in the pretrial order. I hope we can be able to continue along these lines. Yes, counsel for the respondent.

930
02:46:44,820 --> 02:46:49,580
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: Your Honor, may we inquire of the order of presentation for Wednesday next week, Your Honor?

931
02:46:50,100 --> 02:46:55,560
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: It will be Ms. Violeta Constantino, as I understand, and then Ms. Nenita Camposano.

932
02:46:55,860 --> 02:46:56,920
Atty. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: We confirm, Your Honor.

933
02:46:58,380 --> 02:46:59,580
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: In that order, Your Honor.

934
02:47:00,280 --> 02:47:01,560
Atty. Gerville “Jinky Bitrics” R. Luistro: We confirm, Your Honor.

935
02:47:01,820 --> 02:47:02,340
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: In that order.

936
02:47:04,580 --> 02:47:07,200
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Any other matters? There being no other matters—yes, counsel?

937
02:47:07,760 --> 02:47:13,420
Atty. Michael Wesley Poa: No other matters. One other matter, Your Honor. So, more than one witness per day?

938
02:47:13,940 --> 02:47:31,440
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: We will be issuing the subpoena for both. I have no idea if it's going to be a short direct and cross and/or recross. So we shall see. Kindly prepare for the two witnesses on that day. If there are no other matters, the Chair hereby—rather...

939
02:47:32,580 --> 02:47:34,840
Sen. Francis “Chiz” Escudero: Yes, Senator Judge Pia is recognized, ma'am.

940
02:47:34,840 --> 02:47:48,520
Sen. Pia S. Cayetano: Do I assume, given that we seem to be continuing in the same manner of presentation of witness, that I understand the Presiding Officer discussed with Council about changing the order? Is that still on the table, just so we can also prepare?

